---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="MetaFlux — Derivatives, on first principles."
  description="An independent L1 derivatives exchange. Perpetuals, spot and options from one account with one margin number, finality in a single block, a parallel EVM in every block."
  canonical="https://mtf.exchange/"
  script={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script is:inline>document.documentElement.classList.add('js')</script>
<script src="/home.js" is:inline defer></script>
</Fragment>
<Nav />

<header class="hero">
  <div class="status rise">Independent L1 · testnet live</div>
  <h1 class="rise">Derivatives, on<br><em>first principles</em>.</h1>
  <div class="side rise d1">
    <p>Perpetuals, spot and options, cross-margined in one account. Matching and clearing run inside consensus, so a trade settles in the block it prints.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <a class="btn" href="https://app.mtf.exchange/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Trade →</a>
      <a class="more" href="/whitepaper.html">Whitepaper</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="stream rise d2" aria-hidden="true">
  <canvas></canvas>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <section class="sec reveal" id="trade">
    <div class="kicker">Markets</div>
    <div class="head">
      <h2>BTC, ETH, SOL and more, all in one account against a single margin requirement.</h2>
      <a class="btn" href="https://app.mtf.exchange/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Trade →</a>
    </div>
    <ul class="assets" aria-label="Markets, live off the testnet"></ul>
    <p class="assets-note">Live marks from the testnet</p>
    <div class="shot-wrap"><div class="shot"><img src="/shots/desk.webp" width="3720" height="2392" decoding="async" alt="The MetaFlux testnet trading desk: a BTC-USDC perpetual with its candle chart, live order book, order ticket, a four-position blotter and the account summary." loading="lazy"></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec reveal" id="products">
    <div class="kicker">Products</div>
    <ul class="list">
      <li><a href="https://docs.mtf.exchange/products/perpetuals"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="t" cx="8" cy="12" r="6"/><path d="M8 6a6 6 0 1 0 0 12c4 0 5-6 8-6a3 3 0 1 1 0 6c-2 0-3-2-4-3"/></svg><b>Perpetuals</b><span>Linear, USDC-margined, no expiry. Marked to a composite mark price, with funding settled each asset&rsquo;s period. Cross or isolated, one-way or hedge mode.</span><i>→</i></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.mtf.exchange/products/spot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path class="t" d="M4 9h13l-3-4h3l4 4-4 4h-3l3-4z" stroke="none"/><path d="M20 15H7l3 4"/><path d="M4 9h13"/></svg><b>Spot</b><span>A price-time priority order book. Both legs of a fill settle together in the same block, delivery versus payment.</span><i>→</i></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.mtf.exchange/products/options"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path class="t" d="M3 17l6-10 4 8 4-4 4 6z" stroke="none"/><path d="M3 17l6-10 4 8 4-4 4 6"/></svg><b>Options</b><span>European puts and calls, fully collateralized, quoted by RFQ. Puts cash-settle in USDC; calls settle physically in the underlying.</span><i>→</i></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.mtf.exchange/concepts/order-types"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path class="t" d="M3 16h5v-4h5v-3h5V6h3v13H3z" stroke="none"/><path d="M3 19l5-3 5-4 5-3 3-3"/></svg><b>Order types</b><span>Trailing stops, scale ladders, TWAP and chase execution, worked by the matching engine itself.</span><i>→</i></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.mtf.exchange/concepts/portfolio-margin"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path class="t" d="M4 9l8-5 8 5-8 5z" stroke="none"/><path d="M4 9l8-5 8 5-8 5-8-5z"/><path d="M4 13l8 5 8-5M4 17l8 5 8-5" opacity=".5"/></svg><b>Portfolio margin</b><span>Risk-based margin in the style of SPAN. The whole book is stressed across a price and volatility grid, and hedges net. For accounts above 100K USDC.</span><i>→</i></a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="vision">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="reveal">MetaFlux starts from one premise: a derivatives exchange should be a chain, <em>not a contract on one</em>.</p>
    <p class="reveal">The clearinghouse is the state machine. Margin, mark-to-market and liquidation run in consensus, on rules every counterparty can audit.</p>
    <p class="reveal">An EVM shares every block, so vaults and strategies are contracts reading the same book. New listings go to auction, and the winning bid is burned.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Components ship across phased testnet milestones. Where this site describes something not yet live, the whitepaper says when.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap">
  <section class="sec reveal" id="security">
    <div class="kicker">Settlement</div>
    <h2>Settlement finality in one block.</h2>
    <p class="lead">MetaFlux runs its own consensus, MetaFluxBFT. A block commits when validators holding two-thirds of bonded stake sign it, and while less than a third is faulty, a committed block cannot be unwound. There is no reorg risk to price in and no confirmation count to wait for. The leader rotates every round, and a validator that double-signs is slashed 5% of its stake.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec reveal" id="faq">
    <div class="kicker">FAQ</div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>What is MetaFlux, exactly?</summary>
        <p>A derivatives venue that is its own L1, with its own validator set, its own BFT consensus and an EVM in the same blocks. Execution, clearing and settlement happen in one system instead of three.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which parts of this are shipping today?</summary>
        <p>The testnet runs the clearing core, the parallel EVM and the book today. The rest lands in the order the whitepaper sets out, milestone by milestone.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How are liquidations handled?</summary>
        <p>On a ladder keyed to account health, equity over maintenance margin. The first tier is a margin call: resting post-only orders are pulled and the wallet is notified. Below that come partial, then full, closes at a floored limit price, then a liquidity vault as backstop. If an account still ends negative, the default waterfall runs the vault, an ADL haircut on winning positions, the insurance fund and the treasury, in that order.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>When does mainnet launch?</summary>
        <p>Mainnet follows audit and testnet milestones, not calendar dates. The testnet is live and open for integration now; six months of public testnet precede the TGE, with phased validator onboarding and the bridge audit as the explicit gating item.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does integration look like?</summary>
        <p>One gateway serves POST /info, POST /exchange, WebSocket and EVM JSON-RPC. Orders are signed in a standard EIP-712 envelope, so hardware signers and browser wallets work unmodified; agent wallets sign every order and never hold withdrawal authority. The SDKs (TypeScript and Rust, preview) map agent wallets, sub-accounts, vaults, cross and isolated margin and client order ids one to one. <a href="https://docs.mtf.exchange/">Docs →</a></p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who is the testnet for?</summary>
        <p>Anyone. There is no application and no allow-list. Take test USDC from the faucet, point your client at the gateway, and trade. We especially want to hear from market makers and teams shipping production trading systems: <a href="mailto:builders@mtf.exchange">builders@mtf.exchange</a>.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<Footer />
</Base>
